    "result_text": "Done. The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline now rejects a duplicate normalized telephone with **409 Conflict**. I kept structural impact low by adding behaviour as small, single-method units rather than growing any existing class:\n\n**New files (each one cohesive unit, zero surrounding complexity):**\n- `EnsureOwnerTelephoneUnique.java` \u2014 a new step reading the built `@Val Owner`, scanning existing owners via `OwnerRepository`, and throwing when the normalized telephone is already taken.\n- `DuplicateTelephoneException.java` \u2014 a checked exception (mirrors the existing `InvalidTelephoneException`).\n- `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` (mirrors the existing handler pattern).\n- Escalation YAML mapping the exception to the handler.\n\n**One-line-shaped edit:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `ensureUniqueTelephone` step between `build` and `save` (build normalizes the telephone first, so the check compares normalized values under the same transaction).\n\nI did not touch `BuildOwner`, `SaveOwner`, or any other existing function \u2014 the new step slots into the existing `build \u2192 save \u2192 respond` orchestration. The uniqueness check runs after normalization so it correctly compares the digit-normalized telephone the way the seed/API data stores it.",
